        <mxCell id="step-7" value="7" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1312" y="339" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="step-8" value="8" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#FFFFFF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="967" y="339" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="title" value="Regulated bank: hybrid deployment&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-weight:normal&quot;&gt;Where each workload runs, and how Nigerian data stays in Nigeria&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;fontFamily=Arial;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="24" width="1000" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;padding-left:20px;margin-top:10px;margin-bottom:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Nigerian customers&lt;/b&gt; reach &lt;b&gt;core banking&lt;/b&gt; in the primary Lagos data centre.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Core banking and the &lt;b&gt;customer database&lt;/b&gt; share a site, so the round trip stays under 5 ms. No cloud Region can: Lagos to Cape Town is about 4,800 km, at least 48 ms there and back in fibre.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Every transaction is written to an on-premises &lt;b&gt;WORM audit store&lt;/b&gt;, so logs that contain personal data never leave Nigeria.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;The database replicates to a &lt;b&gt;secondary data centre in Nigeria&lt;/b&gt;. Automated failover meets the 15-minute recovery time without moving data abroad.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;AI training on Nigerian data bursts to &lt;b&gt;GPU instances in the AWS Lagos Local Zone&lt;/b&gt; over &lt;b&gt;AWS Direct Connect&lt;/b&gt;. Data stays on &lt;b&gt;EBS&lt;/b&gt; in Lagos, with no snapshots.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EU customers and EU fintech partners&lt;/b&gt; call &lt;b&gt;Amazon API Gateway&lt;/b&gt; in eu-west-1. Partner APIs that carry Nigerian data end in the Lagos data centre instead.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;EU services on &lt;b&gt;AWS Fargate&lt;/b&gt; keep EU personal data in &lt;b&gt;Amazon RDS&lt;/b&gt; in a private subnet (GDPR).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Audit events go to &lt;b&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/b&gt; with Object Lock in compliance mode, so no one can alter or delete them.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;b&gt;Residency rule:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;padding-left:20px;margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Nigerian personal data, its backups and its logs stay in Nigeria.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Only anonymised aggregates cross to eu-west-1.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Identity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;padding-left:20px;margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;One public cloud. &lt;b&gt;IAM Identity Center&lt;/b&gt; federates with the bank&#x27;s on-premises directory, so there is one source of identities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cost:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;padding-left:20px;margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:10px&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;GPUs run on demand, so nothing idles between training runs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Option: &lt;b&gt;AWS Outposts&lt;/b&gt; racks, available in Nigeria, bring AWS APIs on premises.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1500" y="120" width="360" height="880" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
